What: /sys/bus/spi/devices/spiB.C/reset_asserted
Date: October 2026
Contact: Qiyu Project <qiyu@example.invalid>
Description:
        Root-writable reset control, serialized with SPI exchanges. Writing
        1 asserts reset (A081 GPIO115 low); writing 0 releases it (GPIO115
        high). Reading returns the GPIO's logical assertion state. Standard
        boolean strings accepted by kstrtobool are also supported.

        Probe enables power on GPIO41 and leaves reset asserted. Userspace
        releases reset at the camera/radio startup boundary. Changing reset
        does not disable power, unbind the device, close an existing transport
        file, or clear irq_count/transfer_count. An open transport does not
        prevent reset. Removal returns ENODEV. IRQ counts and queued packet
        interpretation remain the userspace owner's responsibility.
